e  place was far from the lap of modern  luxury not that kate couldn't live  without running water or electricity for  long stints of time but it wasn't a  house that had been built recently  although she was no expert in either  archaeology or architecture kate didn't  think anyone had lived there for decades  possibly even centuries it was almost  medieval a single room that was  completely ramshackle practically  falling apart at the seams everywhere  she looked the wood that had originally  been used to build it was either rotting  away or had been broken into splintered  remains plants from the forest had  started growing through the floors and  the walls as if nature was trying to  reclaim this spot of land where someone  had once come to get away from the rest  of the world sighing kat shook her head  as she looked at the dilapidated house  there was no way even she could sleep  there it was too much of a safety risk  parts of the ceiling could easily fall  on her during the night if the wind  picked up enough turning to leave she  stopped in her tracks as she noticed  another structure much smaller behind  the house it had been so dwarfed in size  by the slightly bigger building that it  was completely obscured from view but it  looked to be in much better shape in  terms of its structural integrity it was  a woodshed its front door hanging lazily  open while not exactly brand new by  anyone's standards it was at least far  more intact than the main house taking a  few steps forward kate felt something  like glass crunch under the heel of her  boot she scanned the floor instinctively  checking for any more so as to not  injure herself even with the low amount  of sunlight fading ever rapidly it  didn't look like more kicking her boot  to loosen the shard she made her way  towards the woodshed not noticing that  what she'd been standing on had been a  compass reaching the shed she peered  inside it was pitch black within almost  as dark as the rest of the force would  be in a few minutes taking off her  backpack and setting it down she  searched inside for her flashlight  retrieving it and flipping on the switch  she looked back into the shed and that  was when she saw it taking a step back  cat tripped over her bag scrambling back  up to her feet to make sure she had seen  what she thought she had it was just  lying there still and lifeless for a  split second she hoped it was a trick of  the light just an old decaying lump of  wood but it wasn't it was a body the  remains were charred reduced to little  more than bones some time ago even the  ground next to it looked like it had  been scorched blackened by some intense  fire damage kate's eyes were so  transfixed on the burned mass of bones  that a sudden sound startled her thunder  growled above immediately telling her  she had little choice in what to do next  her options were either she could sleep  outdoors and get drenched by the rain  and possibly catch hypothermia from  being cold and wet or she could spend a  night in the cramped confines of this  woodshed which she would have to share  with a long dead body walking back  outside to retrieve her bag she pulled  out a ground sheet and used it to cover  up the bones it was a mostly sleepless  night and those were a rarity for kate  any sleep she did get was light easily  interrupted by as little as her own  movements and offered her no actual rest  but for the next few hours she just lay  awake on the wooden floor it wasn't the  sounds of rain drumming against the shed  ceiling or the booming of thunderclaps  that were keeping her awake thoughts of  what she was going to do about the bones  kept coming to the forefront of kate's  mind should she report it to the police  when she got to jasper was there even  any point if she had no idea where on  the map this abandoned place was  frustrated she tossed and turned  eventually sitting up as something made  a sound it was a low creaking rusty  metal hinge screeching for a lack of any  oiling over the years the door was open  swinging lazily in the decreasing winds  its lock having long since broken  grumbling to herself kate reached for an  old shovel that had been left in the  shed and went to grab the open door as  her head poked out from the shed she  looked around it was the middle of the  night nothing to be seen anywhere around  yet she couldn't escape the feeling she  was being watched taking the shovel she  damned it underneath the door frame  keeping it closed at last there was  quiet maybe now she'd be able to get  some much-needed sleep and she did but  that's when the nightmare started the  dream was bizarre unlike anything kate  had ever experienced before she  instantly recognized the warm flickering  orange glow of a large fire before her  naturally she started to pace her way  towards it the fire's heat washing over  her the closer she got but as she  approached kade noticed something moving  amongst the flames arms flailed trying  desperately to extinguish the blaze legs  kicking and writhing and that was on top  of the screaming another figure was  standing facing the bonfire their back  to kate as she walked closer still with  every step the sounds of insects buzzing  could be heard getting louder and louder  but it wasn't until she stepped near  enough that she saw where the noise was  coming from a swarm of bugs was darting  through the air hovering around the  other figure there were enough of the  insects that they formed what looked  like a cloak every part of it moving and  buzzing of its own accord the whole  nightmare was so vivid kate had no idea  if it had been brought on by her  exhaustion or that her mind was still  fixated on the bones she'd found in the  woodshed dehydration lack of food or  even some other influence it could have  been any one of those factors that had  caused her to dream a dream like this or  a combination of all of them nonetheless  she could feel the bugs tapping at her  skin as she walked up to the other  figure still unable to see them clearly  the noise of insect wings whizzed past  her ears louder than ever loud enough to  be real putting a hand on the figure's  shoulder kate turned them around it was  a woman or what was left of her she had  huge gaping wounds left by something  that had been cruelly buried in her face  yet somehow she was still standing dead  but also alive at the same time the  swarm of bugs around her moved with her  body as she turned and faced kate a pair  of glassy eyes staring at her they were  both blank completely empty each one  missing its pupil opening her mouth the  woman let out a piercing blood-curdling  shriek all around her the sound of the  bugs got louder almost deafening and as  she screamed so did kate panting and  shuddering she bolted upright shock  racking her entire body hard thudding  against her rib cage instantly the exact  moment she woke up kate realized that  feeling was back she had spent so much  of her time hiking through the woods on  her own that she could tell when someone  was watching her in the dark she fumbled  for her flashlight and clicked it on to  reveal the door was still jammed shut  apart from her there was no one else  inside the shed no one alive at least  looking over her shoulder she could see  the bones behind her and immediately  backed away from them as far as she  could in that tiny wooden hut she had  covered them before going to bed she was  certain of it hadn't she all of a sudden  kate felt her skin start to itch an  intense irritating feeling she had  experienced the effects of poison ivy  and all sorts of plants that caused  similar reactions but this was easily a  thousand times worse her skin felt like  it was burning she scraped her  fingernails down her exposed arm trying  to suppress the itching even for a  moment but it did nothing she scratched  at the other arm over and over again in  one spot until her flesh was pink and  raw still no change 