 for her  flashlight buried under some of the dirt  that had been dug up she pointed it at  the thing she'd found the woman the same  one from her nightmare  something inside her chest moved  scratching sharply causing kate to cough  and once she started she couldn't stop  it was like the itching she felt on the  outside had now worked its way inside  and it was spreading no moving in fact  not just moving but crawling through her  lungs burrowing down into her stomach  and at the same time  upwards the clawing of tiny legs digging  their way up her windpipe blocking it  kate couldn't breathe she dropped to her  knees wretching as she struggled for air  sputtering as she felt something move at  the back of her throat that was when she  heard the buzzing again locusts a swarm  of them came spilling out of kate's  mouth she couldn't scream let alone  catch her breath they filled the shed in  seconds engulfing her entire body as  more and more of the desert bugs still  came pouring from her mouth outside the  wind kicked up again with enough force  to blow the door to the woodshed closed  trapping kate inside with the bugs that  tore at her there was a single word on  the wooden surface of the door written  in deep black charcoal she'd missed it  the door had been opened when she found  the shed the word was which the scp  foundation would later find this cursed  cabin and would naturally lose a number  of d-classes to a horrific form of  locust-based suffocation well there are  clues as to what exactly is going on in  this terrible place from the malice of a  long dead sorceress to the lingering  revenge of a woman wrongfully persecuted  definite answers as to the anomalous  mechanisms of the shed known as scp-4595  still elude even the foundation's finest  minds it's a place so mysterious and  dangerous that the special containment  procedures read for safety purposes no  personnel are permitted to enter  scp-4595  scp-4595 should only be entered by  authorized testing personnel under the  supervision of the scp-4595  research lead under no circumstances is  scp-4595-a to be disturbed in any way so  perhaps we'll never truly know why a  humble wooden shed in jasper indiana  causes such horrifying effects for its  victims the scp foundation thinks it's  safer to just lock it away and forget  about it letting its ancient wood and  old bones rot in the dark but if you are  really curious about the truth you can  always take a walk down the side of the  patoka river and pay the witch a visit  if you're lucky you might even get to  leave now go and check out scp-4000  taboo and  scp-3333 tower to learn more about some  strange landmarks and places that it's  best to avoid next time you go hiking  through the woods on your own
 

